# Keep every text file LF in the working tree as well as in the repository.
#
# Why: without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf rewrites line
# endings and `git status` reports every script modified when nothing was
# edited -- which is how a reviewer comes to distrust their own diff. It also
# breaks the shell scripts outright under WSL or Git Bash, where a `\r` at the
# end of the shebang makes the interpreter unfindable.
#
# The reference statements, the exports and the attestations matter more than
# convenience here: SHA256SUMS and the content-addressed freeze hash file
# BYTES, so a line-ending conversion anywhere in the reference tree changes
# hashes that are supposed to change only when meaning changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.olean binary
*.pem   binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
